# s1-page-http -> CORE-WIRE-G2

- `native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace/Cargo.toml`, `[dependencies]`, after `bytes = { workspace = true }`:
  `http-body-util = { workspace = true }`, `hyper = { workspace = true }`, `hyper-util = { workspace = true }`
  (all three are `[workspace.dependencies]` entries already; the locked graph has them: hyper 1.12.0, hyper-util 0.1.21, http-body-util 0.1.5; no new crate).
  Reason: `pageserver/http.rs` (hyper http1 server connection over `TokioIo`) and `pageserver/serve.rs` (`BoxBody`, `Full`, `Empty`, `BodyExt`).
- Same file, `tokio = { workspace = true, features = [...] }` of `[dependencies]`: add `"net"` (`tokio::net::TcpListener` of the accept loop). The tests use `tokio::net::TcpStream`
  and `AsyncReadExt/AsyncWriteExt`, already covered by the dev-dependency features (`io-util`) once `net` is on.
- Then `cargo update --workspace --offline` (the lock gets the three new edges of mixdog-workspace) and `cargo hakari generate` (workspace-hack already has hyper/tokio-net features).
- `native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace/src/lib.rs`: `pub mod pageserver;` is still the line of `s1-page-policy.wire` (CORE-WIRE-G2 applies it once; nothing more is needed for this task).
- SERVICE_PENDING (`mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs`): this task registers no protocol method; nothing to remove. The task that mounts `PageServer`
  (s1-ws-wire) builds it with `PageServer::new(<data dir>/page-server.port, <PageAuthority over the grant store and project registry>, lanes)`.
